{"type": "sena", "_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "lesson_name", "content": "Good Deeds"}, {"type": "unit_name", "content": "Zero Waste"}, {"type": "position", "content": 6}, {"type": "origin", "content": "stub"}, {"type": "lesson", "content": 13}, {"type": "level", "content": "B2.3"}], "type": "metadata"}, {"contents": [{"type": "test", "content": "false"}], "type": "achievment_test"}, {"contents": [{"type": "primary", "content": "Exchange information about unlikely events or fairly certain conditions that will be fulfilled in present, past or future  in spoken or written texts and in work and social contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_1", "content": "Understands extended speeches, lectures, articles and reports of the professional, academic, or daily life on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear."}, {"type": "secondary_2", "content": "Understands extended speeches, lectures, articles and reports of the professional, academic, or daily life on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear."}, {"type": "secondary_3", "content": "Understands extended speeches, lectures, articles and reports of the professional, academic, or daily life on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear."}, {"type": "secondary_4", "content": "Understands extended speeches, lectures, articles and reports of the professional, academic, or daily life on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear."}, {"type": "secondary_5", "content": "Understands extended speeches, lectures, articles and reports of the professional, academic, or daily life on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear."}, {"type": "secondary_6", "content": "Understands extended speeches, lectures, articles and reports of the professional, academic, or daily life on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear."}, {"type": "secondary_7", "content": "Understands extended speeches, lectures, articles and reports of the professional, academic, or daily life on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear."}, {"type": "secondary_8", "content": "Understands extended speeches, lectures, articles and reports of the professional, academic, or daily life on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear."}], "type": "objectives"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Must, Have to, Had to for What is Compulsory"}, {"type": "describer", "content": " When you want to talk about what is mandatory or required, you can use the modals <span class=\"strong\">must</span>, <span class=\"strong\">have to</span> and <span class=\"strong\">had to</span>. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "You use <span class=\"strong\">must</span> and <span class=\"strong\">has/have</span> to to talk about what is compulsory in the present or future."}, {"type": "text", "content": "For example:<br/> <span class=\"italic\">All travelers to the United States <span class=\"strong\">have to</span> have proper identification.</span><br/> <span class=\"italic\">All changes in the law <span class=\"strong\">must</span> be passed by a majority.</span>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "When you want to talk about something that was necessary or obligatory in the past, you use <span class=\"strong\">had to</span>. You do not use <span class=\"strong\">must</span>, as it has another meaning when used to talk about past situations."}, {"type": "text", "content": "For example: <br/> <span class=\"italic\">When I lived in Japan, I <span class=\"strong\">had to</span> sort my garbage very carefully.</span>"}, {"type": "example", "content": "I realized I have to learn more about zero waste."}, {"type": "example", "content": "We must think more about this."}, {"type": "example", "content": "All discarded materials have to be designed to become resources for other to use."}, {"type": "example", "content": "Zero waste initiatives say that we must eliminate all discharges into the land, water or air that are a threat to planetary, human, animal or plant health."}, {"type": "example", "content": "Governments must write and implement policy and provide subsidies for industries to support them in their efforts to reduce waste."}, {"type": "example", "content": "I had to learn the three Rs in school, reduce, reuse recycle."}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "First Conditional: If and If not "}, {"type": "describer", "content": "You use the<span class=\"strong\"> first conditional</span> to talk about real or possible situations. When you present the condition, it is common to use <span class=\"italic\">if</span>. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "The structure of <span class=\"strong\">first conditional </span>is usually If+present simple (If clause) and will+infinitive (result clause). <br>Remember to use a comma (,) if the If clause is at the beginning of the sentence.<br> For example: <span class=\"italic\">If we don't change the way we deal with waste<span class=\"strong\">, </span>we will destroy the planet.<span><br> <br> You can use other phrases instead of <span class=\"italic\">if</span> or <span class=\"italic\">if not</span> to make your language more varied and sophisticated. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Two alternatives you can use to introduce the condition clause are: <span class=\"italic\"provided that</span> and<span class=\"italic\" so long as</span>."}, {"type": "text", "content": "For example: <br/> <span class=\"italic\"><span class=\"strong\">If</span> you come down from the tree now, I won't call the fire department.<br/> = <span class=\"strong\">So long as</span> you come down from the tree now, I won't call the fire department. <br/>= <span class=\"strong\">Provided that</span> you come down from the tree now, I won't call the fire department.</span>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "<span class=\"italic\">Provided that</span> is more formal than <span class=\"italic\">if</span>. "}, {"type": "example", "content": "If industries have financial motivation and contributions, they will be able to focus on packaging designs, manufacturing processes and material selection that will reduce waste."}, {"type": "example", "content": "If people are more aware of the possibilities for reusing waste to reduce pollution, they will put pressure on their governments to enforce zero waste initiatives."}, {"type": "example", "content": "I think if we all work together, we can really make a difference!"}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "waste "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "unwanted material"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: We produce so much waste! "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn11le13ob06aud01"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "These are words you use to talk about social issues."}], "type": "target_word_describer"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "ethical "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "relating to moral principles"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example:  It's an ethical, economical and efficient way to guide people to change their lifestyles and practices to emulate sustainable natural cycles."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn11le13ob06aud02"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to emulate"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to match; to surpass"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: We emulate people who we admire."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn11le13ob06aud03"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "sustainable "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "able to be maintained"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: We need to find sustainable alternatives."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn11le13ob06aud04"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "discarded "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "thrown away"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: All discarded materials have to be designed to become resources for other to use."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn11le13ob06aud05"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "discharge "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "substance allowed to go into the air, water or land"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Zero waste initiatives say that we must eliminate all discharges into the land, water or air."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn11le13ob06aud06"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "With a partner, come up with an idea for improving the environment in your city or country."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Develop an initiative plan. What will you do? Who will do it?"}, {"type": "text", "content": "How will you do it?"}, {"type": "text", "content": "Make a poster for your plan. Include pictures if possible."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Present your poster and plan to your group."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Listen to the other presentations and as a group, choose the plan that you think is best."}], "type": "takeaway_extension"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "I write an initiative plan with a partner."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I create a poster to demonstrate my plan."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I present my initiative plan to a group."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I help decide on the best plan of the group."}], "type": "takeaway_assessment"}, {"type": "background_image", "content": "engenn11le13ob06re1img01.jpg"}], "labs": [{"exercises": [{"questions": [], "img_path": "", "stimuli_ids": [0], "template_override": 1, "type": "WLC", "_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": "I can talk about social issues, beliefs, opinions and moral or personal dilemmas."}, {"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": "I can express compulsory action."}, {"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": " I can express that a fairly certain condition will be fulfilled."}, {"type": "Free Header Item", "content": " What do you know about waste management in your city?"}, {"type": "Free Header Item", "content": " What more can we do to reduce waste?"}], "type": "instructions"}, {"contents": [{"type": "group_name", "content": "Welcome"}], "type": "group"}, {"type": "feedback", "content": {"incorrect_feedback": [{"type": "text", "content": "try again"}, {"type": "text", "content": "Maybe next time"}], "allowed_attempts": 2, "attempt_feedback": [{"type": "text", "content": "You have 2 tries"}, {"type": "text", "content": "you have 1 attempt left"}], "correct_feedback": "Correct"}}, {"type": "free_header_text", "content": "Ask your partner:"}, {"type": "free_type_text_area", "content": "Where does all that garbage go?"}], "id": 0}, {"questions": [{"_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": ""}], "type": "question"}], "id": 0, "responses": [{"correct": 0, "