, "id": 0, "selected": 0}]}], "stimuli_ids": [], "template_override": 1, "type": "DWS", "id": 11, "_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "Develop an initiative."}], "type": "instructions"}, {"contents": [{"type": "group_name", "content": "Take Away"}], "type": "group"}, {"type": "feedback", "content": {"incorrect_feedback": [{"type": "text", "content": "Whoops! Something important is missing."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Maybe next time..."}], "allowed_attempts": 2, "attempt_feedback": [{"type": "text", "content": ""}, {"type": "text", "content": ""}], "correct_feedback": "Correct!"}}, {"contents": [{"type": "skill", "content": "Speaking"}, {"type": "skill", "content": "Writing"}, {"type": "skill", "content": "Reading"}], "type": "learning_skills"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "Instructions: Complete the following steps. Fill in the Self Assessment."}], "type": "post_instructions"}]}], "type": "scholar", "_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "has_nav", "content": true}, {"type": "has_exercise_controls", "content": true}], "type": "lab_options"}], "id": 0, "stimuli": [{"contents": [{}], "type": "welcome", "_data": [], "id": 0, "template_override": 1}, {"contents": [{"type": "slideshow", "value": {"audiosrc": "engenn11le13ob06re2aud01", "images": [{"time": "0", "text": "", "id": 0, "image": "engenn11le13ob06re2img01.jpg"}, {"time": "100", "text": "As I've been thinking about how I can be the change I want to see in the world, it is becoming clearer how much waste and pollution negatively affect our world. We produce so much waste! Where does all that garbage go? I realized I have to learn more about zero waste. It's a philosophy that encourages the redesign of resource life cycles so that all products are reused. We must think more about this. If we don't change the way we deal with waste, we will destroy the planet.", "id": 1, "image": "engenn11le13ob06re2img01.jpg"}, {"time": "32000", "text": "The zero waste concept recommends a process similar to the way that resources are reused in nature. It's an ethical, economical and efficient way to guide people to change their lifestyles and practices to emulate sustainable natural cycles, where all discarded materials have to be designed to become resources for other to use. Zero waste initiatives say that we must eliminate all discharges into the land, water or air that are a threat to planetary, human, animal or plant health. Eliminating waste from the outset means that industries and governments have to be heavily involved. Governments must write and implement policy and provide subsidies for industries to support them in their efforts to reduce waste.", "id": 2, "image": "engenn11le13ob06re2img02.jpg"}, {"time": "81000", "text": "If industries have financial motivation and contributions, they will be able to focus on packaging designs, manufacturing processes and material selection that will reduce waste. Zero waste also supports finding positive alternatives to landfill and incineration and raising community awareness. If people are more aware of the possibilities for reusing waste to reduce pollution, they will put pressure on their governments to enforce zero waste initiatives. I had to learn the three Rs in school: reduce, reuse, recycle. Zero waste adds one more R: recovery. We will always have waste but we can find new ways to process it.  I think if we all work together, we can really make a difference!", "id": 3, "image": "engenn11le13ob06re2img03.jpg"}], "coverimg": "engenn11le13ob06re2img01.jpg"}}], "template_override": 1, "type": "audio", "id": 1, "_data": [], "title": ""}]}]}